WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.062 --> 00:00:06.805
Sherlock Holmes and I were spending a few weeks in a college town while he researched some obscure subject in a library.

2
00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:10.800
One evening Mr. Hilton Soames came to visit us at our boardinghouse.

3
00:00:10.801 --> 00:00:15.069
We didn't know him well, but he'd always impressed me as a nervous fellow.

4
00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:20.022
When we entered the parlor, he was so agitated that I knew something unusual had happened.

5
00:00:20.023 --> 00:00:25.113
"Please sit down." I gestured toward a chair, but Soames was too excited to sit.

6
00:00:25.114 --> 00:00:30.231
"I know you're a lecturer at St. Luke's College," I said, "but I can't remember your subject."

7
00:00:30.232 --> 00:00:33.430
"He teaches Greek," Holmes replied impatiently.

8
00:00:33.431 --> 00:00:35.479
"Why are you here, Mr. Soames?"

9
00:00:35.648 --> 00:00:38.835
"We've had an unfortunate incident at the college."

10
00:00:38.836 --> 00:00:41.054
Soames wrung his hands in dismay.

11
00:00:42.338 --> 00:00:46.094
"If you weren't in town, Mr. Holmes, I don't know what I'd do.

12
00:00:46.095 --> 00:00:49.643
I hope you can spare me a few hours of your valuable time."

13
00:00:49.644 --> 00:00:54.739
Holmes frowned. "I'm very busy right now and don't want to be distracted.

14
00:00:54.740 --> 00:00:57.209
If you have a problem, call the police."

15
00:00:57.210 --> 00:01:02.060
Soames appeared startled by Holmes' rudeness. I was less surprised.

16
00:01:02.061 --> 00:01:07.502
Away from the comfort of our Baker Street rooms, the famous detective was even grumpier than usual.

17
00:01:07.503 --> 00:01:10.782
"Good-bye." Holmes turned to leave the parlor.

18
00:01:10.783 --> 00:01:14.247
"Please, Mr. Holmes, you're the only one who can help me!"

19
00:01:14.248 --> 00:01:16.542
Soames seemed quite frantic.

20
00:01:16.543 --> 00:01:21.095
"You're more than a great detective. You're also famous for your discretion.

21
00:01:21.095 --> 00:01:28.832
Summoning the police will result in a lot of unwanted publicity—and possibly, a terrible scandal for me and the college."

22
00:01:29.569 --> 00:01:33.943
Heaving a sigh and turning around, Holmes motioned for him to continue.

23
00:01:33.943 --> 00:01:38.914
Soames said that tomorrow was the first day of an exam for a very competitive scholarship.

24
00:01:38.915 --> 00:01:41.803
The winner would receive a huge amount of money.

25
00:01:41.804 --> 00:01:47.639
Soames was in charge of this first portion, which involved translating a chapter from Greek to English.

26
00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:53.494
"As you can imagine," Soames went on, "a great deal of secrecy surrounds this exam.

27
00:01:53.495 --> 00:01:57.105
Absolutely no one can see the Greek text ahead of time.

28
00:01:57.106 --> 00:02:01.525
If a student were to get hold of it in advance, he'd have a huge advantage."

29
00:02:01.526 --> 00:02:05.315
"More than an advantage—he would be cheating!" I said.

30
00:02:05.316 --> 00:02:09.698
"I gather that's what happened?" Holmes asked as the two of us sat down.

31
00:02:10.465 --> 00:02:14.114
Soames gave a miserable nod and dropped into a chair too.

32
00:02:14.115 --> 00:02:19.130
"Around three o'clock this afternoon, the printer delivered proofs of the exam to my rooms.

33
00:02:19.131 --> 00:02:22.720
My job was to correct any mistakes and return the proofs.

34
00:02:22.721 --> 00:02:27.233
Then the final version could be printed in time for tomorrow afternoon's exam."

35
00:02:27.234 --> 00:02:32.318
By four-thirty Soames had not finished reviewing the proofs, but he was meeting a friend for tea.

36
00:02:32.319 --> 00:02:37.195
So he left the three pages of proofs on his desk, carefully locked the door, and went out.

37
00:02:37.196 --> 00:02:41.790
When he returned, he was horrified to see a key in the lock to his door.

38
00:02:41.791 --> 00:02:44.290
"What time was this?" Holmes asked.

39
00:02:44.291 --> 00:02:47.918
"Sometime between five-thirty and six," Soames said.

40
00:02:47.918 --> 00:02:53.613
"My own key was in my pocket, and my servant, Bannister, has the only duplicate."

41
00:02:54.322 --> 00:02:57.981
"And this Bannister," Holmes said, "do you trust him?"

42
00:02:57.982 --> 00:03:03.899
"Oh, yes! He's an older man, who has looked after my rooms for ten years and is completely honest."

43
00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:05.695
Soames returned to his story.

44
00:03:05.696 --> 00:03:10.084
As Soames stood looking at the key, Bannister happened to come down the stairs.

45
00:03:10.085 --> 00:03:13.736
"Oh, there's my key!" Bannister cried.

46
00:03:13.737 --> 00:03:16.059
"I wondered where I'd left it."

47
00:03:16.060 --> 00:03:19.625
"Did you enter my rooms while I was out?" Soames asked.

48
00:03:19.626 --> 00:03:23.400
"Yes, sir. I brought your tea as usual at five o'clock.

49
00:03:23.401 --> 00:03:28.640
When I realized you'd gone out, I removed the tea tray, and I must have forgotten my key."

50
00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:34.904
Soames was angry at Bannister's carelessness but didn't want to scold him on the stairs, where someone might overhear.

51
00:03:34.905 --> 00:03:38.177
He asked Bannister to come into his rooms.

52
00:03:38.988 --> 00:03:44.989
"The moment we entered my sitting room," Soames said, "I knew that someone had tampered with the proofs.

53
00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:49.593
I had left them in a neat pile on my desk, but now they were scattered about the room.

54
00:03:49.594 --> 00:03:54.313
One page was on the floor; another was on a small table by the window.

55
00:03:54.314 --> 00:03:57.444
The third page was still on my desk."

56
00:03:57.445 --> 00:04:01.834
"Oh, really?" Holmes lifted his eyebrows at this new information.

57
00:04:01.835 --> 00:04:05.116
"For a moment I wondered if Bannister had gone through my papers.

58
00:04:05.117 --> 00:04:10.854
But he denied that, and I'm convinced he was telling the truth because he immediately collapsed into a chair.

59
00:04:10.855 --> 00:04:14.456
He was upset that his carelessness has caused me a grave problem."

60
00:04:14.457 --> 00:04:17.423
"Was he all right?" I asked in concern.

61
00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:23.697
"He nearly fainted, and I was feeling dizzy with anxiety myself," Soames said.

62
00:04:23.698 --> 00:04:26.859
"We were both concerned that a student had entered my rooms.

63
00:04:26.860 --> 00:04:29.896
Everyone in the academic world has heard of this scholarship.

64
00:04:29.897 --> 00:04:34.087
Can you imagine how much damage a cheating scandal would inflict upon the college?"

65
00:04:34.088 --> 00:04:38.031
I nodded, picturing the story on the front page of every newspaper.

66
00:04:38.032 --> 00:04:41.679
Soames said there were other signs that someone had been in his sitting room.

67
00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:45.683
On the table by the window, he found some pencil shavings and broken lead.

68
00:04:45.684 --> 00:04:51.755
"The rascal was copying the exam so quickly that he broke his pencil and had to sharpen it!" Soames said.

69
00:04:51.756 --> 00:04:54.699
Holmes rubbed his hands together with glee.

70
00:04:54.700 --> 00:04:57.402
"That was a lucky find, Soames!"

71
00:04:58.515 --> 00:05:03.088
I could tell Holmes was recovering his good humor as he became engrossed in the case.

72
00:05:03.089 --> 00:05:05.500
"That's not all," Soames said.

73
00:05:05.501 --> 00:05:09.327
"My brand-new desk had a three-inch cut in its red leather top.

74
00:05:09.328 --> 00:05:12.222
Not a mere scratch, Mr. Holmes, a cut!

75
00:05:12.223 --> 00:05:15.667
I also found a small piece of what looks like black clay on the desktop.

76
00:05:15.668 --> 00:05:18.162
I've never seen anything like it before."

77
00:05:18.163 --> 00:05:20.939
"Could it be some type of eraser?" I asked.

78
00:05:20.940 --> 00:05:23.737
"No." Soames shook his head.

79
00:05:23.738 --> 00:05:27.029
"It's mixed with specks of a substance like sawdust."

80
00:05:27.030 --> 00:05:32.741
Soames continued to search his sitting room but didn't find any footprints or other signs of the intruder.

81
00:05:32.742 --> 00:05:38.616
"I was unsure of what to do, but then I remembered you were in town," Soames said to Holmes.

82
00:05:39.604 --> 00:05:43.434
"So I locked the proofs in my desk and rushed off to consult you."

83
00:05:43.435 --> 00:05:46.574
"Where is Bannister now?" Holmes asked.

84
00:05:46.575 --> 00:05:49.785
"I was in such a hurry that I left him collapsed in the chair.

85
00:05:49.786 --> 00:05:51.994
He was still upset, poor fellow.

86
00:05:51.995 --> 00:05:56.040
Oh, say that you'll help me, Mr. Holmes!" Soames pleaded.

87
00:05:56.041 --> 00:05:59.650
"If the mystery isn't solved, the exam will be postponed."

88
00:05:59.651 --> 00:06:02.692
"And you'll have a lot of explaining to do," I said.

89
00:06:02.693 --> 00:06:08.524
Soames turned to me. "You can't begin to imagine the number of people who will have to be notified.

90
00:06:08.525 --> 00:06:11.953
There's the head of the classics department, the dean—"

91
00:06:11.954 --> 00:06:14.894
"Well then, we'd better get busy," Holmes interrupted.

92
00:06:14.895 --> 00:06:24.845
"If you can wait a moment, Mr. Soames, we'll fetch our overcoats and set off to examine the scene of the crime."

